	doi = {10.1109/ICCSC66714.2025.11135336},
	shorttitle = {Advancing Route Optimization},
	abstract = {The evolution of Artificial Intelligence from theoretical foundations to practical applications has significantly had an impact on industrial optimization. The Traveling Salesman Problem, a non-deterministic polynomial-time hard problem, is considered a key challenge in logistics and route planning. Classical methods face limitations when large instances of Traveling Salesman Problem are handled giving rise to the adoption of approximate methods, particularly metaheuristics. Including Genetic Algorithms, Simulated Annealing, Ant Colony Optimization, and Particle Swarm Optimization, metaheuristics have been used in different Traveling Salesman Problem variants. Efficient solutions are presented by these algorithms, when exploring an extensive solution space, achieving a balance computational efficiency with solution quality. Their application is evaluated, and the results demonstrate their effectiveness to produce near-optimal solutions while reducing computational effort, especially for complex Traveling Salesman Problem instances. These results reflect the practical value of metaheuristics for real-world optimizing issues.},
